ter supply points using satellite imagery. Losses associated with water supply were modelled after Wiedemann et al. (2015b).", "@type": "Input"}, {"term": {"@type": "Term", "termType": "water", "name": "Water, pumped groundwater", "units": "m3", "@id": "waterPumpedGroundwater"}, "value": [1419.548064], "operation": {"@type": "Term", "name": "Providing animals with water", "termType": "operation", "@id": "providingAnimalsWithWater", "units": "hour"}, "methodClassification": "modelled", "methodClassificationDescription": "Measured water data on-farm were not available and were modelled from an assessment of water supply and utilisation on the farms using water balances, using methods described in Wiedemann et al. (2015b). Sheep drinking water was estimated using the equation determined by Luke (cited in CSIRO 2007). Proportions of drinking water supplied from bores, creeks and rivers or farm dams (Table 1) were determined from the survey and CSF site visits, and were verified by an analysis of water supply points using satellite imagery. Losses associated with water supply were modelled after Wiedemann et al. (2015b).", "@type": "Input"}, {"term": {"@type": "Term", "termType": "water", "name": "Water, river/stream", "units": "m3", "@id": "waterRiverStream"}, "value": [597.7044480000001], "operation": {"@type": "Term", "name": "Providing animals with water", "termType": "operation", "@id": "providingAnimalsWithWater", "units": "hour"}, "methodClassification": "modelled", "methodClassificationDescription": "Measured water data on-farm were not available and were modelled from an assessment of water supply and utilisation on the farms using water balances, using methods described in Wiedemann et al. (2015b). Sheep drinking water was estimated using the equation determined by Luke (cited in CSIRO 2007). Proportions of drinking water supplied from bores, creeks and rivers or farm dams (Table 1) were determined from the survey and CSF site visits, and were verified by an an